# Deploy is human-owned

The agent **edits source only**. You (the developer) build and run.

## Do not

- Run `swift build`, `xcodebuild`, `codesign`, `open …WindowLens.app`, or install to `/Applications`
- Modify or create ad-hoc `.app` bundles under the repo or `/Applications`
- Call `./dev-relaunch.sh`, `killall WindowLens`, or otherwise deploy/restart the app
- Add temporary “agent builds” or dual packaging scripts

## Do

- Change Swift / project / docs as requested
- Leave verification to the developer via **Xcode build** + `./dev-relaunch.sh` (Warp)

## Canonical run path

```bash
./dev-relaunch.sh
```

Builds with `xcodebuild`, syncs to `/Applications/WindowLens.app`, launches.
`--skip-build` relaunches without compiling.

There is no separate `build-app.sh`; do not reintroduce one unless explicitly asked.
